{"assets":["/statement-assets/7f1690281594595c87e48ae81c307fafe0842d02d497e9bc028698ec659ddcc5.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"156","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Mrs. Hudson's Pancakes"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mrs. Hudson hasn't made her famous pancakes for quite a while and finally she decided to make them again. She has learned "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" new recipes recently and she can't wait to try them. Those recipes are based on "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" special spices. Mrs. Hudson has these spices in the kitchen lying in jars "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"numbered"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" with integers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" (each spice lies in an individual jar). Each jar also has the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"price"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the corresponding spice inscribed — some integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We know three values for the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th pancake recipe: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"di"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":". Here "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"di"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":" are integers, and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pattern"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of some integer written in the numeral system with radix "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"di"},{"kind":"text","text":". The pattern contains digits, Latin letters (to denote digits larger than nine) and question marks. Number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"di"},{"kind":"text","text":"-base numeral system "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"matches the pattern"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":", if we can replace question marks in the pattern with digits and letters so that we obtain number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" (leading zeroes aren't taken into consideration when performing the comparison). More formally: each question mark should be replaced by exactly one digit or exactly one letter. If after we replace all question marks we get a number with leading zeroes, we can delete these zeroes. For example, number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"40A9875"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"11"},{"kind":"text","text":"-base numeral system matches the pattern \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"??4??987?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4A9875"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" does not."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To make the pancakes by the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th recipe, Mrs. Hudson should take all jars with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"numbers"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" whose representation in the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"di"},{"kind":"text","text":"-base numeral system matches the pattern "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":". The "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"control number"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the recipe ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"zi"},{"kind":"text","text":") is defined as the sum of number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the product of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"prices"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of all taken jars. More formally: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/7f1690281594595c87e48ae81c307fafe0842d02d497e9bc028698ec659ddcc5.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" (where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":" is all such numbers whose representation in the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"di"},{"kind":"text","text":"-base numeral system matches the pattern "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mrs. Hudson isn't as interested in the control numbers as she is in their minimum prime divisors. Your task is: for each recipe "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" find the minimum prime divisor of number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"zi"},{"kind":"text","text":". If this divisor exceeds "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"100"},{"kind":"text","text":", then you do not have to find it, print -1."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains the single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 104"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The second line contains space-separated prices of the spices "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a0, a1, ..., an - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" is an integer ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai ≤ 1018"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains the single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ m ≤ 3·104"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of recipes Mrs. Hudson has learned. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines describe the recipes, one per line. First you are given an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"di"},{"kind":"text","text":", written in the decimal numeral system ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ di ≤ 16"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Then after a space follows the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":" pattern — a string from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"30"},{"kind":"text","text":" in length, inclusive, consisting of digits from \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"9"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", letters from \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and signs \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". Letters from \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" should be considered as digits from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"15"},{"kind":"text","text":" correspondingly. It is guaranteed that all digits of the pattern (including the digits that are represented by letters) are strictly less than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"di"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then after a space follows an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":", written in the decimal numeral system ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ci ≤ 1018"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Please do not use the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"%lld"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" specificator to read or write 64-bit integers in С++, in is preferred to use "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cin"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cout"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", strings or the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"%I64d"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" specificator instead."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each recipe count by what minimum prime number the control number is divided and print this prime number on the single line. If this number turns out larger than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"100"},{"kind":"text","text":", print -1."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n1\n1\n2 ? 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n2 3 5 7\n4\n2 ?0 11\n2 ?1 13\n2 0? 17\n2 1? 19\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n2\n23\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n1000000000000000000\n1\n16 ?????????????? 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test any one-digit number in the binary system matches. The jar is only one and its price is equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", the number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c"},{"kind":"text","text":" is also equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", the control number equals "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":". The minimal prime divisor of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test there are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" jars with numbers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the prices are equal "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"7"},{"kind":"text","text":" correspondingly — the first four prime numbers. In all recipes numbers should be two-digit. In the first recipe the second digit always is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":", in the second recipe the second digit always is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", in the third recipe the first digit must be "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":", in the fourth recipe the first digit always is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". Consequently, the control numbers ​​are as follows: in the first recipe "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 × 5 + 11 = 21"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the minimum prime divisor is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":"), in the second recipe "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 × 7 + 13 = 44"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the minimum prime divisor is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"), in the third recipe "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 × 3 + 17 = 23"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the minimum prime divisor is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"23"},{"kind":"text","text":") and, finally, in the fourth recipe "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5 × 7 + 19 = 54"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the minimum prime divisor is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test, the number should consist of fourteen digits and be recorded in a sixteen-base numeral system. Number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the number of the single bottles) matches, the control number will be equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1018 + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":". The minimum prime divisor of this number is equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"101"},{"kind":"text","text":" and you should print -1."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"156E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/156/problem/E"}